Art direction job for a Roblox horror game level. Theme (from the owner): a MEGA RETRO 1980s-1990s multiplex cinema that has been ABANDONED and has slipped into "the Backrooms" - liminal, empty, too quiet, humming lights, endless-feeling, slightly wrong. It must look like a still from a film: photoreal, cinematic lighting, rich real materials, NOT a video game, NO people, NO text other than what is described.

Use your built-in image generation tool. Save every image as PNG in the current working directory with EXACTLY the file name given (copy the generated file here). Do NOT run git, do NOT commit, do NOT delete or modify any other file. Final answer: only the list of saved files.

The space (keep this layout in every hero image; the two attached images show it): a very long, wide cinema concourse/lobby hall (about 200 m long, 34 m wide, 10 m ceiling). Two rows of large round columns run down the hall. The left (north) wall has three big auditorium entrances with marquee signs above, framed movie-poster lightboxes and wall sconces between them. The right (south) wall has wide openings labelled CONCESSIONS, ARCADE, RESTROOMS and SERVICE, with small cafe tables along it. The floor is wall-to-wall carpet. Camera: eye level (1.7 m), looking down the length of the hall, 24 mm lens.

Make SIX different directions, A-F. For each direction make 3 images:
  mb_<X>_hero.png    - the concourse in that style (16:9)
  mb_<X>_carpet.png  - the carpet as a flat, top-down, evenly lit, PERFECTLY TILEABLE square texture (no perspective, no shadows)
  mb_<X>_wall.png    - the wallpaper / wall finish as a flat, evenly lit, PERFECTLY TILEABLE square texture

A  "Cosmic Confetti": classic 90s multiplex - near-black carpet with neon confetti, stars and squiggles (teal, magenta, yellow); charcoal textured vinyl walls with a neon stripe band; chrome and mirrored column cladding.
B  "Memphis Pastel 80s": teal/magenta/purple Memphis-pattern carpet (squiggles, triangles, dots); pastel geometric wallpaper; pink neon; faded and dusty.
C  "Deco Revival 1987": burgundy carpet with gold art-deco fans and chevrons; dark red damask flock wallpaper above dark wood wainscot with brass rails; frosted glass sconces.
D  "Backrooms Mono-Yellow": the purest Backrooms feel - damp, stained mustard-beige carpet with a faint repeating 90s cinema pattern (tickets, film reels) almost worn away; faded yellow chevron/stripe wallpaper; buzzing fluorescent light panels; everything slightly yellow and humid.
E  "Popcorn & Reels": deep red carpet with popcorn boxes, film reels and ticket stubs pattern; cream and red striped wallpaper with a film-strip border; warm amber bulbs.
F  "Synthwave Grid": deep purple carpet with a neon triangle/grid pattern; black acoustic panel walls with thin neon strips; magenta and cyan glow; hazy.

All directions share the same story: abandoned for decades - dust, a few stains, a toppled stanchion, dead bulbs, slight haze - but still beautiful and coherent. Consistent camera and layout across the six hero images so they can be compared side by side.

